# 🛡️ Day 1 — Lab Preparation & Environment Setup

> **Project:** Wazuh Honeypot SOC Lab
> **Platform:** Oracle VirtualBox
> **Focus:** Environment preparation and lab planning
> **Status:** In Progress

---

## 🎯 Today's Objectives

* Prepare the GitHub project documentation.
* Inspect the existing Ubuntu virtual machine.
* Check available system resources.
* Plan a safe virtual network for the lab.
* Document the initial environment.

## ✅ Task Checklist

### 01 — GitHub Setup

* [ ] Create the `wazuh-honeypot-soc-lab` repository.
* [ ] Add the main `README.md`.
* [ ] Create the `docs/` folder.
* [ ] Add this Day 1 checklist.
* [ ] Create a `screenshots/` folder for project evidence.

### 02 — VirtualBox Inspection

* [ ] Open Oracle VirtualBox.
* [ ] Locate the existing Ubuntu virtual machine.
* [ ] Check whether the VM starts successfully.
* [ ] Open the VM's Settings.
* [ ] Record the allocated RAM and CPU cores.
* [ ] Check the virtual disk size and available host storage.
* [ ] Take a screenshot of the VM details.

### 03 — Ubuntu Verification

* [ ] Start Ubuntu, if it is not already running.

* [ ] Open the Terminal.

* [ ] Check the operating system:

  ```bash
  cat /etc/os-release
  ```

* [ ] Check memory:

  ```bash
  free -h
  ```

* [ ] Check available disk space:

  ```bash
  df -h
  ```

* [ ] Check network interfaces:

  ```bash
  ip addr
  ```

* [ ] Save the useful outputs in your notes.

### 04 — Security Lab Planning

* [ ] Identify the role of the Ubuntu VM.
* [ ] Decide whether an additional VM will be needed for Wazuh.
* [ ] Plan an isolated network for future honeypot experiments.
* [ ] Avoid exposing vulnerable services to the public internet.
* [ ] Do not change the current network configuration until the lab plan is clear.

### 05 — Documentation & Evidence

* [ ] Add the VM details to the project notes.
* [ ] Save a screenshot of VirtualBox.
* [ ] Save a screenshot of Ubuntu running.
* [ ] Record any errors or questions.
* [ ] Commit the completed notes and screenshots to GitHub.

